{"title":"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Explanation_for_Step_2_of_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Explanation for Step 2 of Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Fast)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Fast)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the tens digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/6167ef088efb35dcdaa7ff1ef5453e2955b04ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/a/08ae88b13a9948035918a8e61598e37ddc81eafd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}~3 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}~5 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}~7 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}~9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We wish to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96337e7fa2a180da19a624c8f61b296f61148d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}\\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"24\" /> and find the tens digit. By the Chinese Remainder Theorem, it suffices to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/2/162d6dad6140d5836180640a8a2a4800c3f3e39e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/6/226b8ad3fabdcc30f8d5ed7aa3d4d3e43794219f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}\\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"24\" /> and find the solution to the system. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acab5583a895652d8f013dec3a3726ae3cdffff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}\\equiv 0\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" />, so we just need to find the remainder modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>By Euler’s Totient Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/c/1fcaf55768ae1040eed21643cfbc67c6ad65546c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}\\equiv 6^r\\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"24\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f14793ae9472364b477a5af230d98fc3fa2792.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\equiv 6^6\\pmod{\\varphi(25)=20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"201\" height=\"21\" />. Hence we need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b1093b003d241b5d01bbdd37a78d5c033d25d10d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^6\\pmod{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Now we again use the Chinese Remainder Theorem. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/d/8bd4c5769a92bbf369b7520ebe7526299689adbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^6\\equiv 0\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"124\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea83cfbc51c371714d38874a713eceda2faa12ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^6\\equiv 1^6\\equiv 1\\pmod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"21\" />. Testing cases yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/7/a37e97c44695c8c4fc29ad913dc941f1ed555593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^6\\equiv 16\\pmod{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"142\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e5ec5a7c91a397ada543ea921f885ba85e84c96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}\\equiv 6^{16}\\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"24\" />. Now we can simplify:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fde8b18550dedbfc4fcae5b63c082a6a5899f0d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6^{6^6}\\equiv 6^{16}\\equiv (6^4)^4\\equiv 1296^4\\equiv (-4)^4\\equiv 256\\equiv 6\\pmod{25}\\]\" width=\"444\" height=\"22\" />\nSolving the system <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/6/c068ea423af657ab58946248b033f64023b9aa00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}\\equiv 6\\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"24\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acab5583a895652d8f013dec3a3726ae3cdffff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}\\equiv 0\\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/c/43c1afc2c6a81fc20397a6bfd87552acbf926851.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}\\equiv 56\\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"158\" height=\"24\" />. Hence the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf325847c927d5e502a3609eb4a32778eb722da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Eevee9406\">eevee9406</a>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Explanation_for_Step_2_of_Solution_1\">Explanation for Step 2 of Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Explanation for Step 2 of Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>For coprime integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, there is a specific identity that's a direct consequence of Euler's Totient Theorem, which is probably what the author used: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/c/52cfeb76b00e1b1f470e816a63f8d05a9885e8c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^{b}\\equiv a^{b \\mod(\\varphi(n))}\\pmod{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"209\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>To show how the identity works in this case, the theorem directly tells us that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f9005b6d679b16158785ea95e8ce0e976bcf1d61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{20}\\equiv 1\\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"21\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/6/776a6c10a7cbc46485e94ac8a8e22fb1e248c43f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\varphi(25)=25\\cdot(1-\\frac{1}{5})=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"203\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Logically, in order to apply this relationship, it's convenient to define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/8/ad82578603b96121a2a497fde195bdb050980d21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^6=20k+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are integers. By definition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cfd24b048123d461b9c1d1166eda40a09c31519.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r\\equiv 6^6\\pmod{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"21\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the remainder when divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. So:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddf42dd6c67ee11b343f830aecbe94fb684c7149.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6^{6^6}\\equiv 6^{20k}\\cdot6^r\\equiv (6^{20})^k\\cdot6^r\\equiv 1^k\\cdot6^r\\equiv 1\\cdot6^r\\equiv 6^r\\pmod{25}\\]\" width=\"470\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>~iambaconiamgod\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/1/2a144ab6125fadb30696b3240c2c750e53829966.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6} = 6^{46656}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" />\nNow, listing out the first few values of the rightmost two digits for power of 6, we get\n</p><p>06, 36, 16, 96, 76, 56, 36, 16, 96, 76, 56, 36...\n</p><p>Now, note that the pattern starting from at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8406a2a50c1aa1040c8862b912a5f3d703d9569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> will continue. Treating the first as a 56 since it won't matter for the result, the pattern turns to 56 every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b79ad925edbf4d70632ab6808a32fab214e8b07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1+5k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a non-negative integer. So, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/e/f0e89d7c84014b4ff8d4aa941f305b3b4c223155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46656 = 1 + 5(9331)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />, it will have 56 as its rightmost 2 numbers, giving the answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf325847c927d5e502a3609eb4a32778eb722da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>-Failure.net (minor latex edit by Voidling)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Fast.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Fast)\">Solution 3 (Fast)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Fast)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Trying the first few powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives a pattern with period <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/a/22a505acd8b49dc62df0777366b90fdc94b17b09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[06, 36, 16, 96, 76, 56, 36, \\dots \\Rightarrow 0, 3, 1, 9, 7, 5, 3, \\dots\\]\" width=\"373\" height=\"16\" />\nNotice any power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> has a units digit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/d/47db36e710c7efb1aa9d901cf00a6df1ef4138f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^6 \\equiv 1 \\mod{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" /> and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/f/7cf325847c927d5e502a3609eb4a32778eb722da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C)}~5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"56\" height=\"30\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/3/353f68d49261d6db166aede2d54212312e0b17a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^1$\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" />'s tens digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/2/4225e9b708e3da8a270ce19f6a1cd06629927baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{1+5n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" /> for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/8/578cf6c5b8058f6f8e6369416da6dcaf73f8fc01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> its tens digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> according to our pattern).\n</p><p>~Pearl2008\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/0/fa0c43e6c3a43b95894127804aed1003e87b5526.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[6^{6^{6}} \\pmod{100}\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p>is the desired result. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/1/a51d0842ed0d5db1a36681955bd5534812bfd5e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^6 \\pmod{100} = 64 \\cdot 729 \\pmod{25} \\equiv 14 \\cdot 4 \\pmod{25} \\equiv 56 \\pmod{25} \\equiv 6 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"657\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/7/e87a3c21d7658b70874fee27ee53355244f5d6a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"92\" height=\"20\" /> so two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d37744c06f0912356f89f8a8569d6d46630297e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\equiv 6\\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/c/a2c1203d71f5856d39d062e47595cbbf6b5f26db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\equiv 0 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" />. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/e/86e5aa4be0e49db3f527d405cfe70b94928993d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa1d8c6caa7b0bf2ac223a9baf58c0c1dfc62716.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_1 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/05915304563c4d019596fedd7ff4c1509c31fce6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N_2 = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"17\" /> and in addition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/5/185f4ef61e32a0facc0ea9b7b104c96111f652de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x_1 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"20\" /> is satisfied for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/f/ddfb82e434afc5200828e10f2b75600c6acaa5e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/f/58fb02244e2f372fd19355336d29c446a295b43d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" />, so the smallest solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/5/be516bda57a855a017af9c57522752d415db27cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 19  \\pmod{100} = 56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"197\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>So we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc00df17b29510e58a5b3dc9d0a0cde790f691f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{56} \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"115\" height=\"21\" /> which is finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/0/5e0e2d81a21acac61c8e5f67f1077e5db53b5ef5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{56} \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17d0ac4356225d8ab64bce35028b7c5fcd17c9d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{56} \\pmod {4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"21\" />. The latter is 0, so the former is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/983c621d9d131a64227fe67c981357303c50d953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{16} \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"21\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59ccd52f28da767fe4411bbd3135b34a341a2d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{16} \\cdot 3^{16} \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"143\" height=\"21\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/8/02810f9bfe7b80bf52c2cda235dc1b6f14488804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{10} \\equiv -1 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"19\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a15040be4aa379ba494d972a181c6981da2bf077.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{16} \\equiv -64 \\pmod{25} \\equiv 11 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"287\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3c94eb589540e9205cf58a695a746964dc8b003.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{3} \\equiv 2 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"133\" height=\"21\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b97aa345467553a8e8965c66850c977fe2ffa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3^{16} \\equiv 2^5 \\cdot 3 \\pmod{25} \\equiv 21 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"293\" height=\"21\" /> so we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/0/0c07c1b5dff2a8846bc700c920fb601300107e44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{16} \\equiv 231 \\pmod{25} \\equiv 6 \\pmod{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"272\" height=\"21\" />. Once again, through Chinese Remainder Theorem our <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/b/34be7e52f631196bc5a158aa52dc852a3bddafad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_i = 4, 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> respectively and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/3/b03f3ea7375cf323ed9042fae6712172b27d99f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x_1 = 1 \\pmod{25} \\implies x_1 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/5/1058440cb507b95cdc7bbd2e0bbaff6f1a633748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_2 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"125\" height=\"20\" /> so the smallest solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/9/f8906a9cc4fec1e068abf309f32b62d6b6cb7f59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot 19 \\cdot 4 \\equiv 56 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"197\" height=\"20\" /> so the hundreds digit is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897a203bdf45af36f2b9edc59c3bc0beeb898be1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Writing out the last two digits of the first few powers of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/6/7f6fb99999ef5e817e96137cad5278235c4b3e57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$06, 36, 16, 96, 76, 56, 36, 16, 96, 76, 56, 36.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"314\" height=\"17\" />\nWe can see that the tens digit repeats in cycles of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, beginning at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8406a2a50c1aa1040c8862b912a5f3d703d9569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. We can rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/6/6167ef088efb35dcdaa7ff1ef5453e2955b04ff9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"20\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/0/0900117736bcef508996a3cdc756164511dec8fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{(5+1)^6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" />. By the binomial theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/4/ca46e77b9ea9ce3db54019ecbf6ab341413b7085.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5+1)^6 = \\binom{6}{0}5^6 + \\binom{6}{1}5^5 + \\cdots + \\binom{6}{5}5 + 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"366\" height=\"55\" /> Every term except the final <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f13d282a77a81f7ccc1669e5bcc5232d530ea0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5+1)^6 = 5k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Using the multiplicative property of exponents, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/1/3c161fbc555c1c28186030e53a86dcbd8bc8d239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6} = 6^{5k+1} = 6^{5k}\\cdot 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"160\" height=\"20\" /> Since the last two digits repeat every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> powers starting at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e8406a2a50c1aa1040c8862b912a5f3d703d9569.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bb79ff0d99e2455ebb5e7d69f91113836efef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5k+1\\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" />, we can replace the exponent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8dbfce8b1d8a84e90ccdfa22bd366615595cc8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5k+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, which has the same remainder modulo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a025f3ca942f179479a1189197d9777eaae7bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^{6^6} \\equiv 6^6 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"156\" height=\"24\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/6/2f66a5082a24faa7f80aeec3a6dbb5cc896e6469.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^6 \\equiv 56 \\pmod{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"151\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>~Grigori5040\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B\">2025 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2025 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017042800\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.057 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.167 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 599/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2296/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 156/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18454/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.188      1 -total\n 55.98%    7.942      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 42.27%    5.997      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:34883:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017042800 and revision id 293717. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}